{
	"name": "SquadPanel",
	"_doc": "The squad panel (src/client/SquadPanel; user 2026-11-06: \"add an extra panel that let's players join a squad ... make squads max 6 ... the status of the squad\"), Field Grimoire's notebook like the settings menu: one sheet of map paper folded in two. Left page: the title, your squad (its rune and name, how many of Config/Squads.Max) and each member under it, their name over their status (Config/Squads.Status: a small diamond and the words in the status's ink), an open slot as a dim line; Leave below. Not in a squad: a line saying so in place of the members, no Leave. Right page: your army's squads, one row each (`Row1` is the template, cloned per squad down a scrolling list): rune, name, count, one diamond per member in its status ink, and Join (an ink block) or the words Yours / Full; New squad at the foot. Opened from the loadout menu's Squad button (src/client/Menus) or the Squad key (Config/Settings Key_Squad, J) in the field; Esc, the key, X or a click outside close it. Sizes in reference pixels at theme.scale.referenceHeight, one UIScale, never taller than the GUI area less theme.fitMargin. Colours: Config/Palette UI.Grimoire.Notebook. Desktop only.",
